//? Title: Stable merge sort
//? Subtitle: Actual front comparisons, buffer writes and original payload order
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Sorting records by a key should preserve the input order of records whose keys
are equal when stability matters. Merge sort splits balanced ranges and merges
their sorted children, taking the left front on ties. We expose actual canonical
comparisons and writes, retain the original eight values and seven keyed
records, and separate variable comparison counts from mandatory merge-copy work.
)

\toc

> Derive the stable merge

Use half-open ranges [lo,hi), splitting at lo+floor((hi−lo)/2). A range of
length at most one is sorted. Recursively sort both children, then compare their
current fronts. Take the right front only if its key is strictly smaller;
otherwise take the left front. Drain the remaining run once either child is
exhausted. Write every chosen item into a reusable scratch buffer, then copy the
complete merged interval back.

At each selection, the smaller remaining front is the least remaining item, so
induction proves sorted output. Within a child, items are consumed in their
existing order. On equal keys, every left-child item originally preceded every
right-child item, so selecting left preserves their cross-child order. Induction
from singleton leaves therefore proves stability. Payloads move with items but
never enter the comparison.

The canonical implementation serves the integer sort, keyed-pair sort, analysis
and trace APIs. The report contains no second instrumented sort. Captured
comparisons and both kinds of writes are actual producing operations.

> A tiny real equal-key decision

Use keyed records(2,0),(1,1),(2,2),(1,3), where the second field is an
observable payload. The real merge encounters equal fronts; strict
right-before-left is false, so left wins. The output table retains the actual
moved payloads.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/merge_sort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/merge_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::merge_sort_pairs_trace({{2, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 2}, {1, 3}});
    auto tie =
        std::find_if(t.comparisons.begin(), t.comparisons.end(), [](auto &c) {
        return c.left_key == c.right_key;
    });
    std::print("| actual sorted position | actual key | actual carried payload |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.output.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, t.output[i].key, t.output[i].tag);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("left", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual left-front key\n{}", tie->left_key)).node(
        "right", {6, 0},
        std::format("Actual right-front key\n{}", tie->right_key)).node(
        "choice", {12, 0},
        std::format("Actual strict-right result\n{}; left wins tie",
                    tie->take_right)).edge("left", "right").edge("right",
                                                                 "choice");
    d.save_svg("build/merge_sort_tiny.svg");
}
```
