> Original keyed records: stability is observable

The retained original records are(3,0),(1,1),(3,2),(2,3),(1,4),(3,5),(2,6).
Their payloads are input positions. Sorting by key yields key1 tags1,4; key2
tags3,6; key3 tags0,2,5. Those are original order within each key group, even
though the complete tag sequence is not sorted. General payload values need not
be increasing: stability preserves their prior order rather than sorting the
payload numerically.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/merge_sort_stability.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/merge_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::merge_sort_pairs_trace(dm::algorithms::merge_sort_demo_pairs());
    std::print("| actual sorted position | key | actual original-position payload |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.output.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, t.output[i].key, t.output[i].tag);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    for (std::int64_t key : {1, 2, 3}) {
        std::vector<double> x, y;
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.output.size(); ++i)
            if (t.output[i].key == key) {
                x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(t.output[i].tag);
            }
            p.points(x, y, std::format("key {}", key),
                     key == 1 ? dm::graphics::RGB{37, 99, 235} : key == 2
                     ? dm::graphics::RGB{22, 163, 74}
                     : dm::graphics::RGB{220, 38, 38});
    }
    p.x_label("actual sorted output position").y_label("actual original-position payload").title("Original keyed records: payload order within equal keys").save_svg("build/merge_sort_stability.svg");
}
