> Bound comparisons and account for every write

Merging two nonempty runs of total length m uses at most m−1 key comparisons,
but always m scratch writes and m copyback writes. Every child split is balanced
independently of input values. The worst comparison recurrence and its closed
form are:

$$
W(n)=W(\lfloor n/2\rfloor)+W(\lceil n/2\rceil)+n-1,
\qquad W(n)=n\lceil\log_2 n\rceil-2^{\lceil\log_2 n\rceil}+1.
$$
\alttext(The worst comparison count adds both child counts and at most n minus one comparisons; the closed form uses the ceiling of log base two.)

Take W(0)=W(1)=0. The bound is attainable, but sorted or reverse input is not
automatically a worst-case witness. Summing mandatory merged lengths gives
W(n)+n−1 writes in each phase for n>=1. Therefore total time is Theta(n log n)
on every input for this implementation without presorted-run shortcuts, despite
differing comparison counts. Buffer storage is O(n), recursion depth O(log n),
and returned/captured copies add their separately stated storage.

The bound helper computes integer ceil-log2 and checked wide arithmetic,
throwing if the result cannot fit size_t. Ordinary counters also reject wrap.
Optional capture counts two owned N-item endpoints and every actual
comparison/write/commit record. Default cap one million; zero disables it.
Endpoint admission precedes copying, then each real record is admitted before
its operation. Fields, capacities, scratch/runtime storage and bytes are
excluded. Complete history uses O(n log n) records; a quota failure returns no
prefix.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/merge_sort_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/merge_sort.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, observed, bound;
    std::print("| prescribed n | actual sorted-input comparisons | actual reverse-input comparisons | worst " "comparison bound | actual scratch writes per run | actual copyback writes per run |\n| ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64}) {
        std::vector<std::int64_t> input(n);
        std::iota(input.begin(), input.end(), 0);
        auto a = dm::algorithms::merge_sort_analyze(input);
        std::reverse(input.begin(), input.end());
        auto b = dm::algorithms::merge_sort_analyze(input);
        auto w = dm::algorithms::merge_sort_comparison_bound(n);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, a.work.comparisons,
                   b.work.comparisons, w, a.work.scratch_writes,
                   a.work.copy_writes);
        x.push_back(n);
        observed.push_back(a.work.comparisons);
        bound.push_back(w);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, observed, "sorted comparisons", {37, 99, 235});
    p.line(x, bound, "worst bound", {220, 38, 38});
    p.x_label("prescribed input length").y_label("actual comparisons or exact worst bound").title("Actual comparisons and exact worst bound").save_svg("build/merge_sort_work.svg");
}
```
