\caption(Actual comparison counts and exact worst-case bound.)
\alttext(Prescribed sorted/reverse sequences are controls, not claimed worst-case witnesses; tables also expose mandatory writes.)

> Verification and references

Native tests enumerate every ternary-key sequence through length seven, verify
sorted values and stable original identities, compare keyed payloads with an
independent stable reference, and replay every real comparison, scratch write,
copyback write and merge commit from owned input. Every distinct permutation
through length seven attains the closed-form maximum over the exhaustive set.
Original15 comparisons/24 writes per phase, full-width integer keys, nonmonotone
payloads, empty/singleton cases, exact quotas and ownership are checked. The
shared ten-report batch passes 71 CTest cases, 29 directly instrumented
ASan/UBSan cases, 130 compiled and executed public examples, 598/598 scoped
documentation definitions and ten representative hovers. Independent Python
arbitrary-precision, hashlib, sorted-window, RNG, polynomial, graph and
full-assignment references verify 224,229 actual records. Frozen comparisons
preserve ordinary legacy outputs, including selected clique identities, original
density graphs and memetic partitions. Twelve checkout headers and twelve
identically installed headers compile independently; an installed-header native
consumer links and runs. All four complete programs and all four native figures
pass execution and visual review, and HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed
results and identical image bytes. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-224-233/`.

See Knuth, *The Art of Computer Programming*, Volume3: *Sorting and Searching*,
for merging and merge sort. The stability proof, actual tie convention and exact
balanced-tree count are derived here. The report distinguishes actual canonical
execution from theory and does not substitute a second sorting implementation
for measured results.
